--- !u!114 &-4749358647145894421
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "In this step, you\u2019ll add a <b>Rigidbody</b> component to
      the <b>Block</b> GameObject. \n\nInitially, the block won\u2019t move when
      hit by the ball, acting like an immovable brick wall. This behavior is due
      to the lack of a <b>Rigidbody</b> component, which governs the physics properties
      of the GameObject. \n\nWith a <b>Rigidbody</b> component, the block can react
      to a collision and fall over."
--- !u!114 &-4180886532182521969
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "You\u2019re about to begin the construction of your block tower.
      \n\nTo make your first building block, you\u2019ll start by adding a primitive
      cube. Just like you did with the sphere, you\u2019ll add it to the scene, rename
      it, then reset its position to the origin as a starting point.\n\nHowever,
      this time you\u2019ll use a new technique for creating the new 3D object and
      a new technique for resetting the object\u2019s position."
--- !u!114 &-3716248356803658144
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "In this step, you\u2019ll address the clutter in your Unity
      project's <b>Hierarchy</b> window caused by numerous <b>Block</b> prefabs.
      \n\nYou'll learn to organize these blocks under a single parent GameObject,
      simplifying your scene and making it more manageable. \n\nAs a reminder, a
      <b>parent</b> GameObject is a GameObject that serves as a container for other
      GameObjects, known as <b>child</b> GameObjects. These terms describe a hierarchical
      relationship, much like a family tree."
